---
layout: layouts/base.njk
permalink: /services/
title: "Services — Local SEO, websites & Google Ads | Narrow Digital"
description: "Local SEO, hand-coded websites, Google Ads, reviews and tracking for small businesses in Yucaipa, Banning and the Inland Empire. Every quote priced by hand."
---

{# ==========================================================================
   SERVICES
   All copy lives in src/_data/services.json so the homepage teaser and this
   page never fall out of sync. Edit that file, not this one.
   ========================================================================== #}

<!-- ============ PAGE HERO ============ -->
<section class="page-hero">
  <div class="wrap" data-reveal-group>
    <span class="eyebrow reveal">Services</span>
    <h1 class="reveal" style="margin-top:1rem;">
      Everything that gets a local business found and called<span class="diamond" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede reveal">
      Built for small businesses and the trades &mdash; glass companies, plumbers, HVAC,
      landscaping, and everyone else who lives off the next phone call.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ SERVICE LIST ============ -->
<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="rows" data-reveal-group>

      {% for s in services.items %}
        <div class="row reveal" id="{{ s.slug }}">
          <span class="row__num">{{ s.num }}</span>
          <span class="row__title">{{ s.title | safe }}</span>
          <div class="row__body">
            <p>{{ s.summary }}</p>
            {% for para in s.detail %}
              <p style="margin-top:0.9rem;">{{ para }}</p>
            {% endfor %}
            <ul class="tags">
              {% for d in s.deliverables %}<li>{{ d | safe }}</li>{% endfor %}
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ PRICING ============ -->
<section class="section section--alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="split" data-reveal-group>
      <div class="reveal">
        <span class="eyebrow">Pricing</span>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <h2>Every quote is priced by hand</h2>
        <p class="mt-4">
          There is no price list on this page because there is no set price. A one-truck plumber
          who needs a Google Business Profile straightened out and a shop that needs a new site
          with ads running behind it are different jobs. Charging them the same would mean
          overcharging one of them, and I am not interested in doing that.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4">
          So I look at what the work actually takes, and I set the number myself &mdash; fairly,
          and with your situation in front of me. You get the price and what is included before
          anything starts, and it does not move afterwards unless you ask for something we did
          not agree on. If the honest answer is that you do not need what I do yet, I will tell
          you that instead.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4"><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Ask for a quote</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ FAQ ============ -->
{# Questions live in src/_data/faq.json — edit them there, not here. Each one
   is a native <details> element, so it opens without any JavaScript and still
   works if a script fails to load. #}
<section class="section section--tight">
  <div class="wrap">

    <div class="section-head reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Questions</span>
      <h2>The things people ask before they call</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="faq" data-reveal-group>
      {% for item in faq.items %}
        <details class="faq__item reveal">
          <summary class="faq__q">
            {{ item.q }}
            <span class="faq__icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="faq__a">
            <p>{{ item.a }}</p>
          </div>
        </details>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4 reveal muted small">
      Something not covered here?
      <a class="link" href="/contact/">Ask me directly</a> &mdash; I&rsquo;ll give you a straight answer.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{#
  Structured data for the questions above. This is what lets Google show the
  answers directly in the search results. It is generated from the same JSON
  file as the visible list, so the two can never disagree — which is exactly
  what Google requires.
#}
<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": [
    {%- for item in faq.items %}
    {
      "@type": "Question",
      "name": {{ item.q | dump | safe }},
      "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": {{ item.a | dump | safe }} }
    }{% if not loop.last %},{% endif %}
    {%- endfor %}
  ]
}
</script>

